      "status": "completed",
      "text": "Fulcrum’s late session had ended an hour ago. The streets of the district were nearly deserted by one in the morning. A single bicycle passed by without a headlight. The light rain had stopped an hour ago, and the sidewalks were wet and slick. Mara walked beside Jonah. They had not spoken in thirty minutes. She looked toward him and saw a little crease between his eyes. She had seen it before, at the end of a long day. She turned toward the dark windows. The light of a streetlight caught a raindrop on her jacket and made her think of a diamond. She touched her chest, where she kept her silver cross.",
